{"id": "EUVD-2026-103929", "enisaUuid": "63f7c11a-8fd3-33ba-95e1-57ec280998e7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: ade9000: handle Phase C dip events in IRQ1 handler\n\nADE9000_ST1_CROSSING_DEPTH is the exclusive upper bound for scanning the\nSTATUS1 event bits, so a value of 25 left out the highest event bit,\nADE9000_ST1_DIPC_BIT (bit 25). Phase C dip events were never reported.\n\nBump the value to 26 so bit 25 is scanned.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f73b94acc7ec81f9c49feb87f649ba5a80a0905c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d338af069f08658f53231adb445ddb10048730ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fafefa925ed7ec10383d9bf0378abf878b7f13cb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98675", "GHSA-qpvq-cwgm-ghf8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18865834-8996-3eb2-90f1-d7f390fb9376", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "81de7b4619fc3682a3bedaa7e8d6b2d67ab4e10a <f73b94acc7ec81f9c49feb87f649ba5a80a0905c"}, {"id": "2b540b44-e7f0-31ae-95c1-22a0165dda9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2e1e6a24-f13f-399c-897f-087e41103c84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "444e21ba-a526-3f94-aa8f-0d502b529d9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "81de7b4619fc3682a3bedaa7e8d6b2d67ab4e10a <fafefa925ed7ec10383d9bf0378abf878b7f13cb"}, {"id": "599bf3d1-3dd5-3120-8e80-c78c7795f508", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "6682e5c0-b149-3047-bd6d-389b8b431af8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "6fb368ef-e6de-31f9-9739-e6a92761dc0f", "product": {"name": "Linux